frozen_problem.statement:
There are two known ways to bound Rouquier dimension of a category
\begin{enumerate}
\item bound length of a resolution of a diagonal
\item the minimal depth of a presentation of $\mathcal{C}$ as hocolim (cats with Rouquier dimension $Q$). Meaning if $F:I^{\leq}\to Cat$ diagram with $Rdim F(i)=0$, then $Rdim(hocolim F i)\leq depth(I)$
\end{enumerate}

Can (1) be used to bound (2) or vice-versa?
